.th TROFF I 1976
.sh NAME
troff  \*-  format text
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd troff
[ options ] [ files ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Troff
formats text for a Graphic Systems phototypesetter
according to control lines embedded
in the text files.
It reads the standard input if
no file
arguments are given.
An argument of just ``\-'' refers to the standard input.
.s3
The options, which may appear in any order so long as they
appear before the files, are:
.s3
.ft I
.lp +9 8
option	meaning
.ft R
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-o\fIlist\fR	Print only pages whose page numbers appear
in \fIlist,\fR which consists of comma-separated numbers and number ranges.
A number range has the form \fIN-M\fR and means pages \fIN\fR through \fIM\fR;
a initial \fI-N\fR means from the beginning to page \fIN\fR;
and a final \fIN-\fR means from \fIN\fR to the end.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-n\fIN-\fR	Number first generated page \fIN\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-s\fIN\fR	Stop every \fIN\fR pages.
.it Troff
will stop the phototypesetter every \fIN\fR pages,
produce a trailer to allow changing of cassettes, and will resume after the
phototypesetter START button is pressed.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-m\fIname\fR	Prepends the macro file \fB/usr/lib/tmac.\fIname\fR to
the input \fIfiles\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-r\fIaN\fR	Register \fIa\fR (one character) is set to \fIN\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-i\fR	Read standard input after the input files are exhausted.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-q\fR	Invoke the simultaneous
input-output mode of the \fBrd\fR request.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-t\fR	Direct output to the standard output instead of the
typesetter.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-f\fR	Refrain from feeding out paper and stopping phototypesetter
at the end of the run.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-w\fR	Wait until phototypesetter is available, if currently busy.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-b\fR	\fITroff\fR will report whether the phototypesetter is
busy or unavailable.
No text processing is done.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-a\fR	Send a printable (ASCII) approximation of the results to the
standard output.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-p\fIN\fR	Print all characters in point size \fIN\fR while retaining
all prescribed spacings and motions, to reduce phototypesetting elapsed time.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB-g\fR	Prepare output for the Murray Hill Computation Center
phototypesetter and direct it to standard output.
.i0
.dt
.s3
Each option is invoked as a separate argument; for example,
.s3
	\fBtroff -o\fI4,8-10 \fB-w\fI \fB-m\fIabc file1 file2\fR
.s3
requests formatting of pages 4,8,9 and 10 of a document contained in files
named \fIfile1\fR and \fIfile2\fR,
waits for the typesetter to become available,
and invokes the macro package \fIabc\fR.
.s3
.it Troff
may be used as a filter.
.sh FILES
.dt
